 "derived_from": [],
 "is_vocab": false,
 "stimulus_html": "<p>According to <a href=\"https://openstax.org/r/mba_com\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\"> the Graduate Management Admission Council (GMAC)</a>, the mean score on the GMAT (an entrance exam for graduate schools in business management) is 565, with standard deviation 116. For the LSAT (an entrance exam for law schools),  <a href=\"https://openstax.org/r/kaptest_com\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">Kaplan</a> informs us that the mean score is 150 with standard deviation 10.</p>",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 528625,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "What is the <span data-math=\"z\">z</span>-score for a GMAT score of 715?\n",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "1.29"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "If <i>x</i> is a member of a normally distributed dataset with mean µ and standard deviation σ, then the standardized score for <i>x</i> is <span data-math=\"z = \\frac{{x - \\mu }}{\\sigma } = \\frac{{715 - 565}}{{116}} = \\frac{{150}}{{116}} \\approx 1.29\"></span>.\n"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 528626,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "At what percentile is an LSAT score of 166?",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "94.5th"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>In an empty cell of Google Sheets, use the function NORM.DIST.</p>\n<p>NORM.DIST(your data value, your mean, your standard deviation, TRUE)</p>\n<p>Using your data: =NORM.DIST(166, 150, 10,TRUE)</p>\n<p>You will see the decimal version of the percentile: 0.9452007083</p>\n<p>Convert the decimal to an approximate percentage: the 94.5<sup>th</sup> percentile</p>\n"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 528627,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Which is better: a GMAT score of 650 or an LSAT score of 161?",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "An LSAT score of 161 is better"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Find the percentile score for both scores.</p>\n<p>GMAT of 650:</p>\n<p>In an empty cell of Google Sheets, use the function NORM.DIST.</p>\n<p>NORM.DIST(your data value, your mean, your standard deviation, TRUE)</p>\n<p>Using your data: =NORM.DIST(650, 565, 116,TRUE)</p>\n<p>You will see the decimal version of the percentile: 0.7681471684</p>\n<p>Convert the decimal to an approximate percentage: the 76.8<sup>th</sup> percentile</p>\n<p>LSAT of 161:</p>\n<p>In an empty cell of Google Sheets, use the function NORM.DIST.</p>\n<p>NORM.DIST(your data value, your mean, your standard deviation, TRUE)</p>\n<p>Using your data: =NORM.DIST(161, 150, 10,TRUE)</p>\n<p>You will see the decimal version of the percentile: 0.8643339391</p>\n<p>Convert the decimal to an approximate percentage: the 86.4<sup>th</sup> percentile</p>\n<p>The GMAT score is at the 76.8<sup>th</sup> percentile and the LSAT score is at the 86.4<sup>th</sup> percentile. The LSAT score is better.</p>\n"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
